  <div class="preview-text">
    <p>The MPU6050 tracks linear acceleration and angular velocity. The on-board Digital Motion Processor (DMP) can fuse this data to provide precise roll, pitch, and yaw angles.</p>
    <p>In OpenHW Studio, the sensor features a <strong>Live Data HUD</strong>. Right-click the component on the canvas during simulation to manipulate gravity, rotation speed, and temperature in real-time.</p>
    <div class="tags"><span class="tag">I2C Interface</span><span class="tag">Accelerometer</span><span class="tag">Gyroscope</span><span class="tag">Temperature</span></div>
  </div>
</div>
<h2>Pin Reference</h2>
<table>
  <tbody><tr><th>Pin</th><th>Type</th><th>Description</th></tr>
  <tr><td>VCC</td><td>Input</td><td>Power supply. Typically works on 3.3V or 5V (board has LDO regulator).</td></tr>
<tr><td>GND</td><td>Input</td><td>Ground. Connect to Arduino GND.</td></tr>
<tr><td>SCL</td><td>Input</td><td>I2C Clock. Connect to Arduino A5.</td></tr>
<tr><td>SDA</td><td>Bidirectional</td><td>I2C Data. Connect to Arduino A4.</td></tr>
<tr><td>XDA / XCL</td><td>Bidirectional</td><td>Auxiliary I2C lines to connect external magnetometers (optional).</td></tr>
<tr><td>ADO</td><td>Input</td><td>I2C Address Select. LOW = 0x68 (Default). HIGH = 0x69.</td></tr>
<tr><td>INT</td><td>Output</td><td>Interrupt pin. Used when DMP data is ready (optional).</td></tr>
</tbody></table>
